sers/mcampo84/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcampo84/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcampo84/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcampo84/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcampo84/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mcampo84/teleport_challenge/pulls/5","html_url":"https://github.com/mcampo84/teleport_challenge/pull/5","diff_url":"https://github.com/mcampo84/teleport_challenge/pull/5.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/mcampo84/teleport_challenge/pull/5.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"# Description\r\n\r\nAdd `JobManager` and `Job` types, test for basic functionality.\r\n\r\n* `StartJob` will start a job with the provided parameters and begin logging the output of the job to a buffer which can subsequently be read by multiple clients simultaneously, without blocking.\r\n* `StopJob` will stop a job in progress.\r\n* `StreamOutput` will stream the output of a job to an output source, starting with the log buffer, and continuing through to live output lines until the job is complete.\r\n* `GetStatus` returns the status of a job - whether it is initializing, running, done or has reached an error state.\r\n\r\nSince I don't yet have cgroups set up for the application, I'm intentionally omitting that functionality at this time. Once that is in place, I'll be able to add it to the `JobManager` and test.\r\n\r\nResolves #3 ","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mcampo84/teleport_challenge/issues/5/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mcampo84/teleport_challenge/issues/5/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mca